  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Finely chop brown onion and garlic.\n• In a medium saucepan, melt the butter with a dash of olive oil over medium heat. Cook onion until softened, 3-4 minutes.\n• SPICY! This spice blend is mild, but use less if you're sensitive to heat. Add garlic, Tex-Mex spice blend and tomato paste and cook, until fragrant, 1-2 minutes. Add basmati rice, the water and vegetable stock powder, stirring to combine. Bring to the boil, then reduce heat to low and cover with a lid.\n• Cook for 12 minutes, then remove from heat. Keep covered until rice is tender and water is absorbed, 15 minutes.\n• TIP: The rice will finish cooking in its own steam, so don't peek!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67e23af5c5233ff27ac0a536/step-c60a0400.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• While the rice is cooking, add haloumi to a medium bowl and cover with water to soak.\n• Slice kernels off corn cob.\n• Finely chop tomato and cucumber. Roughly chop coriander.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67e23af5c5233ff27ac0a536/step-b5675010.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Heat a large frying pan over high heat. Cook corn kernels until lightly browned, 4-5 minutes.\n• Transfer charred corn to a medium bowl.\n• To the bowl with corn, add tomato, cucumber, coriander and a drizzle of white wine vinegar and olive oil. Toss to combine. Season to taste.\n• TIP: Cover the pan with a lid if the corn kernels are \"popping\" out.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67e23af5c5233ff27ac0a536/step-2a105820.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain haloumi and pat dry with paper towel. Cut haloumi into 1cm-thick slices.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67e23af5c5233ff27ac0a536/step-d9c8f330.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• When the rice has 5 minutes remaining, return frying pan to medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil.\n• Cook haloumi until golden brown, 1-2 minutes each side.\n• Remove pan from heat and add a drizzle of honey, turning haloumi to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67e23af5c5233ff27ac0a536/step-a9617240.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide Mexican rice between bowls.\n• Top with charred corn salsa and haloumi.\n• Dollop over light sour cream to serve. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/67e23af5c5233ff27ac0a536/step-82745750.jpg"
    }
  ]
